# LoadZone Product Direction

Near-term staff product north star. Full prose: [`docs/agents/product-direction.md`](../../docs/agents/product-direction.md). Vocabulary: [`CONTEXT.md`](../../CONTEXT.md).

## ICP and promise

- Design staff (`apps/app`) for **preparador físico** (División de Honor / Juvenil).
- **Success = less time in the app.** Maximum UX (fewer clicks, fields, decisions) — **not** staff gamification.

## Opinionated defaults

- Plan around **Match Day** (**MD**, **MD-1**, **MD-2**, …) and **Microcycle**.
- Staff **consume** LoadZone-prepared **Exercise** / session content; do not add staff “create Exercise” UX in this wave.
- **Session** calendar: minimal create form; drag-and-drop reschedule; **mobile-first**.
- Prefer defaults over new config/builders.

## Carga

- Primary load-analysis surface label: **Carga** (Spanish UI).
- Prefer interactive tables (microcycle, acute/chronic load, minutes rankings) **inside** the app over “export to Excel and calculate.”
- CSV export may stay as escape hatch — not the main path for load insight.

## Decision test

If two designs compete, pick the one that saves preparador time, speaks MD/microcycle, works on phone first, uses prepared content, and deepens **Carga**.
